1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:02,042
So we’ve prepared
some compost materials,

2
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:03,669
so you guys can
try it yourselves.

3
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,672
I’ll partner up with Jao.

4
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:06,840
[JAO]
It's just amazing how...

5
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:10,218
the more I discover how
knowledgeable you are.

6
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:12,553
And I find your
intelligence...

7
00:00:12,554 --> 00:00:13,555
very attractive.

8
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:15,098
[LEXI] Do you know
what that’s called?

9
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:18,226
[LEXI] Which, incidentally, is
happening right here, right now.

10
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:20,270
They've got chemistry, bro.

11
00:00:20,311 --> 00:00:22,272
I’m Quinito.

12
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:24,315
Today’s story
is about...

13
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:25,483
Inoy.

14
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:27,234
On the island of Siargao,

15
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,861
he met many friends.

16
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:31,280
Goodbye,
my friend, pearl.

17
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:32,614
Do you like libraries?

18
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:35,242
You should see the
New York Public Library.

19
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:38,954
You’ve been to all the
libraries you mentioned?

20
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:42,082
You know, someone messaged me,
looking for a Song Ji Hoon.

21
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:42,709
[PEARL] Who’s that?

22
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,042
[KARA]
Sorry about Archie.

23
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:46,045
He’s a little blunt.

24
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,087
[LEXI]
I doubt it.

25
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:50,091
Well, since I'm leaving
anyway, whatever.

26
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,009
Bye, Kara!

27
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,552
[JAO] I like seeing
you like this, Kara.

28
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:55,346
The love you have for
Siargao is really inspiring.

29
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:57,097
I’m happy that
you’re here, Jao.

30
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:58,808
I’m thankful you came back.

31
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:05,148
- Does he smell good?
- [KARA LAUGHS]

32
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:06,107
Like baby powder?

33
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:08,610
Doesn’t he always look like
he smells like baby powder?

34
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,444
[CAROL STAMMERS]

35
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:12,571
- You go, girl! I’m proud of you!
- [KARA LAUGHS]

36
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:13,573
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]
Good morning.

37
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:14,657
[CAROL]
Hm?

38
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:15,658
[CAROL SNICKERING]

39
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,786
[CAROL AND KARA CHUCKLE]

40
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:19,120
[CAROL AND JAO CHUCKLE]

41
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,246
What’s the occasion?

42
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:22,665
Nothing. I just wanted
to give you flowers.

43
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,250
[JAO]
And don’t worry,

44
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:28,171
I asked permission from the
owner before I picked them.

45
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:33,051
- [KARA CHUCKLES]
- [CAROL GIGGLING]

46
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:35,094
Did you ask the plant, too?

47
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:38,681
- [JAO] Oh, man…
- [KARA CHUCKLES]

48
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:40,642
Just kidding.
Do we have plans today?

49
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:42,310
Not really.
Uh… here.

50
00:01:42,352 --> 00:01:44,646
I just wanted to
make you breakfast.

51
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:46,189
And here.

52
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:48,608
It's just black coffee.

53
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:49,651
No sugar.

54
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,236
Thank you.

55
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:53,738
[CAROL CLEARS THROAT]
All right.

56
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:55,073
[JAO]
Hey!

57
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:56,323
Where are you going, Carol?

58
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:57,449
Aren’t you joining
us for breakfast?

59
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:58,034
[CAROL EXHALES]

60
00:01:58,076 --> 00:01:59,076
Nope.

61
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:01,787
- I don’t want to get in the way.
- [JAO] Oh, please.

62
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:04,582
But I’ll take some Vitamin C to go.

63
00:02:04,624 --> 00:02:05,624
[JAO AND KARA LAUGH]

64
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:06,750
[CAROL]
Smell you later!

65
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:09,254
- [JAO LAUGHS]
- [CAROL GIGGLES]

66
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:12,507
Should I pick you
up after your tour?

67
00:02:13,049 --> 00:02:15,051
No, it’s okay!

68
00:02:16,344 --> 00:02:17,846
When will I
see you again?

69
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,056
On...
Saturday!

70
00:02:21,057 --> 00:02:22,392
Katig’s anniversary.

71
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:24,644
Saturday’s so far away.

72
00:02:26,145 --> 00:02:27,146
[JAO]
How about this?

73
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:29,815
I'll drive you
around all day today,

74
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:33,027
so you can focus
on your tours.

75
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:33,987
Deal?

76
00:02:34,153 --> 00:02:36,364
Jao, I’m not used
to being babied.

77
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:39,784
Nothing has to
change just because...

78
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:44,664
Okay.

79
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:46,499
Thank you.

80
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:49,794
I respect your timeline.

81
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,631
[JAO]
So...

82
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,758
I guess I’ll go talk
to the plant.

83
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:56,843
Go ahead.
[KARA LAUGHS]

84
00:02:57,468 --> 00:02:58,469
[JAO LAUGHS]

85
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:00,054
Did you read the note?

86
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:03,308
“Smell me now,
dye me later”?

87
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:04,892
I put a lot of
thought into that.

88
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,394
- With a smiley?
- [JAO] Yes.

89
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:11,316
[ALON BY JL]

90
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:27,392
[HAN BIN EXHALES]

91
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:56,545
“Dear Admission Committee,”

92
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:57,963
"I’m writing…"

93
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:59,465
You smell so good, sir!

94
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:00,842
What?

95
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,470
You smell really fresh.

96
00:05:05,304 --> 00:05:06,097
Like…

97
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:07,640
mint!

98
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:10,268
Oh, actually,

99
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:14,605
I have this very unique ritual
when I need to concentrate.

100
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:18,568
I always brush my teeth
before a brainstorming session.

101
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:20,110
It clears the mind.

102
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:22,822
Intense freshness gives focus.

103
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:27,410
You’re almost there, Pearl.

104
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:29,579
You have the right words.

105
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:32,749
You just need the
confidence to say it.

106
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:34,416
Well...

107
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:36,544
I will finish this
some other time.

108
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:40,006
I just need to get ready
for our celebration later.

109
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:43,092
But I’ll make sure to
brush my teeth first.

110
00:05:43,843 --> 00:05:45,344
Okay.
Go ahead.

111
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,679
[PEARL CHUCKLES]

112
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:53,019
- It’s still warm!
- [ARIEL] It is!

113
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:54,812
[KARA]
Hold on!

114
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:56,481
- Hi, Kara!
- [KARA] It's aligned, right?

115
00:05:56,522 --> 00:05:57,607
Ariel, give Kara a hand.

116
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:58,941
[ARIEL]
Okay, you got it!

117
00:05:58,983 --> 00:06:00,984
- [PEARL] Oh, right! Hold on.
- [ARIEL] Wow!

118
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:02,194
[JAO]
Kara!

119
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:03,112
[CAROL]
Not like that!

120
00:06:03,154 --> 00:06:07,116
[PEARL] Katig’s
anniversary should be fun!

121
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:08,743
[CAROL]
I hope they like it.

122
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:09,786
There you go!

123
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:11,828
[CAROL]
He likes this, right?

124
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:13,122
[HAN BIN]
Good morning, guys!

125
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:14,248
- [HAN BIN SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Morning!
- [PEOPLE] Morning!

126
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:15,666
- [HAN BIN SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Morning!
- [PEARL] Hi, sir!

127
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:16,793
[JAO]
Happy anniversary!

128
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:17,835
Look, Jao.

129
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:19,753
- You haven't tried this yet, right?
- Cover it for now, Carol,

130
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:20,921
- before the flies get to it.
- [PEARL] There!

131
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:22,047
Yes!
I’m taking care of it.

132
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:23,381
- [PEARL] Let’s bring this outside, too.
- [CAROL] Leave it to me.

133
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:24,592
- [PEARL] Yes!
- [CAROL] Very good nice!

134
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:25,926
- [CAROL LAUGHS]
- [KARA] Later, we should...

135
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:30,055
- [PEARL] Let’s crush the peppers more.
- [CAROL] I agree. Like this.

136
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:31,057
- [PEARL] Yes!
- Need help?

137
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,475
- [PEARL] Wait, this is all that's left.
- I'm okay.

138
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:35,103
I'm just removing
the stray threads.

139
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:38,356
- [CAROL] Go ahead, open it.
- [PEARL] Wow! Yes!

140
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:40,983
- [HAN BIN] Peppers here.
- [PEARL] Yes.

141
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:44,779
You see this?

142
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:49,492
[KARA]
That’s because of you.

143
00:06:50,993 --> 00:06:52,036
You see them?

144
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:57,750
[KARA] They all have
jobs because of you.

145
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:04,090
And you see this
crazy girl right here?

146
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:07,593
This crazy girl has
a job that she loves

147
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,762
and a business that
she’s passionate about

148
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:11,889
because of a
crazy guy like you.

149
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:16,727
[SIARGAONON]
Thank you very much, Han Bin.

150
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:23,234
[GUEST CHATTING]

151
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:24,318
Um...

152
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:27,238
That's fine.
This is good, too.

153
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,781
- [JAO] Need help?
- [PEARL] Hold on, we can just...

154
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:32,577
You guys all mean so much to me.

155
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,413
Thank you, Kara.

156
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:40,918
- I told you so.
- [ARIEL] Here, Jao.

157
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,128
- We'll fry that.
- [PEARL] It’s this one.

158
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:44,172
[JAO] Give it here so we
have room for the food.

159
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:45,882
[CAROL]
I'll put this here.

160
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:47,175
[PEARL]
Orange?

161
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:51,553
- [LOUD MUSIC PLAYING]
- [CROWD CHEERING]

162
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:54,973
[CROWD CHEERING]

163
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:55,975
Wow!

164
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:58,019
[CROWD CHEERING]

165
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:01,647
[CROWD CHANTING]

166
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:05,109
[CROWD CHANTING AND LAUGHING]

167
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:11,949
[CROWD CHEERING]

168
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:12,991
[JAO]
Let’s go!

169
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:16,537
[CROWD CHANTING]

170
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:17,662
- [ARIEL] Han Bin oppa!
- [CROWD CHEERING]

171
00:08:17,663 --> 00:08:20,082
[JAO]
Mr. Han, come on!

172
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:31,135
[CROWD CHEERING AND LAUGHING]

173
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:31,844
[JAO]
Okay, next!

174
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:33,679
[CROWD GROANING]

175
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:36,514
[ARIEL] Guys, it’s just a power
outage. We’re used to that.

176
00:08:36,515 --> 00:08:39,018
Let’s just turn
on our flashlights!

177
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:39,769
[JAO]
That works.

178
00:08:39,770 --> 00:08:40,770
[ARIEL]
See? That's it.

179
00:08:40,811 --> 00:08:41,687
Keep going!

180
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:43,022
- [CROWD CHANTING]
- [JAO] Keep going.

181
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:48,610
[CROWD CHANTING]

182
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:50,320
[JAO]
Let’s go!

183
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:52,948
[CROWD CHANTING]

184
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,075
[LOUD MUSIC RESUMES]

185
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:55,243
[CROWD CHEERING]

186
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,284
[JAO]
Wait!

187
00:08:56,285 --> 00:08:58,788
- [PEARL] There!
- The party’s back on!

188
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:00,414
[CROWD CHEERING]
Yes!

189
00:09:00,456 --> 00:09:03,333
- [PEARL] Kara! Kara!
- [ARIEL] Kara!

190
00:09:03,334 --> 00:09:10,090
[CROWD]
Kara! Kara! Kara!

191
00:09:10,091 --> 00:09:11,300
[JAO]
Smooth moves!

192
00:09:13,844 --> 00:09:15,011
- [PEARL] Tantan!
- [ARIEL] Tantan!

193
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:16,137
[CROWD CHEERING]

194
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:19,516
[CROWD]
Tantan! Tantan! Tantan!

195
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:22,770
[CROWD LAUGHING]

196
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:24,105
[JAO]
Pearl!

197
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:25,690
[CROWD]
Go, Princess Pearl!

198
00:09:25,731 --> 00:09:29,777
[CROWD CHANTING]
Princess Pearl! Princess Pearl!

199
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:33,905
[CROWD]
Lower! Lower! Lower!

200
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:36,200
[CROWD LAUGHING]

201
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:38,244
[JAO]
Who’s next? Ariel!

202
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:39,870
[CROWD CHANTING]

203
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:40,705
[PEARL]
Hey!

204
00:09:40,706 --> 00:09:42,915
- [ARIEL GRUNTS]
- [CROWD LAUGH]

205
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:43,957
[JAO]
Just like his mother.

206
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,000
Definitely,
like mother, like son.

207
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:46,669
Like mother, like son.

208
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,086
Carla’s next!

209
00:09:48,087 --> 00:09:50,089
[CROWD]
Carla! Carla! Carla!

210
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:52,465
[CROWD CHEERING]

211
00:09:52,466 --> 00:09:54,885
Hey! It’s Quinito!

212
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,262
- Quinito!
- Hi, guys!

213
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:59,265
We miss you here!

214
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:00,099
- How’ve you been?
- [QUINITO] Don't say that.

215
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:01,517
You’re giving me FOMO.

216
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:02,059
[QUINITO CHUCKLES]

217
00:10:02,101 --> 00:10:04,061
I mean, I hope to
see you guys soon.

218
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:05,813
Happy anniversary.

219
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:06,938
- Thank you!
- Bye!

220
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:09,650
- Come back, bro! We miss you!
- [QUINITO] Soon, brother. I promise.

221
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:12,485
- Bye! Take care!
- [QUINITO] Bye! Enjoy the party!

222
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:13,696
Bye.

223
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:15,323
[JAO]
Let’s keep it going.

224
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:17,950
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

225
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:19,701
Kara and Jao next!

226
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:25,999
[CROWD]
KaraJao! KaraJao! KaraJao!

227
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,126
[PEARL]
Lower!

228
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:28,252
[CROWD]
KaraJao! KaraJao! KaraJao!

229
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:29,502
[CROWD LAUGHING]

230
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:31,505
[JAO AND KARA LAUGH]

231
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,216
Tantan!
Bonfire, right?

232
00:10:34,258 --> 00:10:36,260
- Bonfire, right?
- Bonfire, right?

233
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:38,595
Hey, Tantan.
Is this your kid?

234
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:39,597
Sir Jao...

235
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:43,059
Uh...
He's a street kid.

236
00:10:43,642 --> 00:10:46,562
I usually give him food
whenever I see him.

237
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,565
So I brought him here.
Hope that’s okay.

238
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:51,859
Sure.
No problem.

239
00:10:52,526 --> 00:10:54,320
Uh, Egay…

240
00:10:54,362 --> 00:10:55,946
this is Sir Handsome.

241
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:58,991
You can also call him, Sir Jao.

242
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:01,243
Isn’t he handsome?

243
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:03,371
[JAO CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
You goofball.

244
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:05,623
Hi, Egay.
Have you eaten yet?

245
00:11:07,291 --> 00:11:09,292
Tantan, can you please
get him something to eat?

246
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:11,087
- Okay, Sir Handsome.
- Thank you.

247
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:17,760
[SIARGAONON]
Your name’s Egay?

248
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:22,973
Tantan told me...

249
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:26,143
you don’t have
a place to stay.

250
00:11:27,895 --> 00:11:30,189
- Where do you sleep?
- In a hut.

251
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:33,316
Where are you
from anyway?

252
00:11:33,317 --> 00:11:34,944
Claver, Surigao.

253
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:36,946
Claver?

254
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,365
That’s pretty far.

255
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:40,991
That’s on another island, right?

256
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:45,287
Where are your parents?

257
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:47,164
My dad passed away.

258
00:11:48,332 --> 00:11:51,419
- And your mom?
- She left me.

259
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,548
[SIARGAONON]
Where did she go?

260
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:58,717
I don’t know.
She just left.

261
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:06,599
How did you end
up here in Siargao?

262
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,228
My dad used to always
talk about Siargao.

263
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:12,606
He grew up here,
so I came here.

264
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:14,650
I’m staying here now.

265
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:18,070
My dad said
it’s beautiful here.

266
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:22,198
Isn’t your mom
looking for you?

267
00:12:22,199 --> 00:12:25,202
Why would she?
She already left me.

268
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:31,167
I’m all alone.

269
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:33,961
But the people in
Surigao are kind.

270
00:12:34,086 --> 00:12:36,589
They let me stay
in their homes.

271
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:39,091
And they give me food.

272
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:40,843
Like Uncle Tantan.

273
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:47,266
You’re not alone, Egay.

274
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:50,644
We’ll help you.

275
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:55,566
Starting today, you can
call me Uncle Jao, too.

276
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:57,693
Sounds good?

277
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:02,406
Do you go to school?

278
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:07,036
Do you want to?

279
00:13:08,829 --> 00:13:09,830
Yes, sir.

280
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:13,626
I can help you go to school.

281
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:17,004
I’ll help you chase your dreams,
whatever they may be.

282
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:21,717
But you have to promise me
you’ll study hard.

283
00:13:23,677 --> 00:13:26,180
You have to work hard
and stay disciplined.

284
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,225
And most importantly,

285
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,644
don’t give up.

286
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:36,065
No matter how
hard life gets...

287
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,817
No matter how cruel
the world can be...

288
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:41,862
don’t give up.

289
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:46,450
You’ll always have
people to help you.

290
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:02,299
- Pearl.
- Yeah?

291
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:05,886
Did you finish your
application form?

292
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:12,059
Thank you so much,
Sir Han, okay?

293
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:16,772
It’s just that…

294
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:19,525
I don’t know what to
talk about in my essay.

295
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,737
And also, the scholarship is…

296
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:27,156
a shot in the dark.

297
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:29,743
What do you mean?

298
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:30,995
[PEARL CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

299
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:32,997
It means impossible.

300
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:36,208
It’s impossible for me to…

301
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,960
[PEARL SIGHS]

302
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:40,462
…get accepted
into that university.

303
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,048
And also...

304
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:45,301
I’m scared.

305
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,261
I’m scared to do it.

306
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:50,014
I understand.

307
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:55,394
But there’s no
harm in trying, Pearl.

308
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:58,606
Just do it.
Do it even if it’s scary.

309
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:03,193
How about you?

310
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:06,405
Have you ever
tried something?

311
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:09,533
Or have you ever
tried doing something

312
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,993
that scared you?

313
00:15:11,201 --> 00:15:13,704
Yes.
Many times.

314
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:16,582
- Really? Like what?
- Yeah.

315
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:19,543
Like…

316
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:22,296
skydiving in Dubai,

317
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:24,423
bungee jumping in New Zealand…

318
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:26,883
and eating balut in Manila.

319
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:28,886
[PEARL AND HAN BIN LAUGH]

320
00:15:29,678 --> 00:15:31,095
Sir Han!

321
00:15:31,096 --> 00:15:34,892
You and your world adventures.

322
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:37,936
You know what,
sometimes, I wonder

323
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:40,856
why you even chose
to stay here in Siargao.

324
00:15:42,941 --> 00:15:44,735
You really love it that much?

325
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:04,797
Yes.

326
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,340
Very much.

327
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:14,890
[LOUD MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:16,934
[HAN BIN CHUCKLES]

329
00:16:16,975 --> 00:16:18,352
[HAN BIN SIGHS]

330
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:22,022
This is why
I lasted 10 years

331
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:25,651
and will go on for another
10 years and beyond!

332
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:27,736
[PEARL]
Hm...

333
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,738
You like the dancing?

334
00:16:29,988 --> 00:16:31,865
No.
The celebration.

335
00:16:31,907 --> 00:16:33,200
The celebration?

336
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:34,618
- Yeah.
- [PEARL CHUCKLES]

337
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:35,660
[HAN BIN]
See...

338
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:38,872
nobody celebrates
life better than Filipinos.

339
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:45,504
And I feel that more
here in Siargao.

340
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:48,340
Come to think of it,

341
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:50,883
maybe that’s the
real Siargao Curse.

342
00:16:50,884 --> 00:16:52,719
People don’t leave the island

343
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,723
because they want to
celebrate life every day.

344
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:01,395
[HAN BIN] They celebrate
life through music.

345
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:06,316
They celebrate life
by enjoying the sea.

346
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:12,239
They celebrate life
through family, friends.

347
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,701
They celebrate life through…

348
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,452
- [PEARL SIGHS]
- ...love.

349
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:19,455
[PEARL]
Thank you so much, Sir Han.

350
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:23,833
Thank you for
celebrating your

351
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:27,838
wonderful, mysterious,
and crazy life with us.

352
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,966
[HAN BIN AND PEARL LAUGH]

353
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:33,677
[PEARL SPEAKS SIARGAONON]
Thank you so much…

354
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:36,096
[PEARL SPEAKS SIARGAONON]
...for loving Siargao.

355
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,021
And most importantly,

356
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:45,689
thank you.

357
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,775
Because now,

358
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:51,528
I have something to
talk about in my essay.

359
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:53,739
You!
[PEARL LAUGHS]

360
00:17:53,947 --> 00:17:55,741
- Me?
- [PEARL] Yes, you!

361
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:56,991
- [PEARL LAUGHS]
- No, no, no!

362
00:17:56,992 --> 00:17:57,493
I...

363
00:17:57,534 --> 00:18:00,536
You have to talk about
yourself in the essay.

364
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:02,247
That’s the whole point.

365
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:04,374
They want to know
your story.

366
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:09,421
Well, you’re part
of my story, Sir Han.

367
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:16,470
[USAD BY CUATRO]

368
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,643
- It’s beautiful, right?
- Yeah.

369
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,270
And your story’s beautiful, too.

370
00:18:25,687 --> 00:18:26,688
Tell me more, okay?

371
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:28,315
[HAN BIN AND PEARL LAUGH]

372
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:30,608
What are you even doing?
Let’s go.

373
00:18:30,609 --> 00:18:31,819
- [RECEPTIONIST] Later.
- Let’s go over there.

374
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:32,945
[RECEPTIONIST]
I’m busy, Kara.

375
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:34,488
- That can wait!
- Good evening, sir.

376
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:35,905
[MAN]
Um...

377
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,199
Do you have a
room available?

378
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:38,659
[RECEPTIONIST]
Sorry, sir.

379
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:39,910
[MAN]
Caitlyn?

380
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:01,306
Sorry, I don’t think
Kara wants to talk to you.

381
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:02,933
This is none of
your business, man.

382
00:19:04,184 --> 00:19:05,184
[ARIEL] Mom!

383
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:06,812
I’ll handle this, okay?
You stay here.

384
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:08,396
I didn't know all of this.

385
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:11,232
[HAN BIN] When I met Kara,
she was already Kara.

386
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:14,236
How can you
not know, Sir Han?

387
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:15,278
[JAO]
Kara?

388
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:17,781
[KARA CRYING SOFTLY]

389
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:20,617
Why is he here?
Is he looking for me?

390
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:23,453
- Kara.
- [KARA BREATHES SHAKILY]

391
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:25,372
[CAROL]
It’s been over seven years.

392
00:19:26,081 --> 00:19:28,292
[CAROL]
Jao’s outside waiting for you.

393
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:29,835
You don’t have
to say anything.

394
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:32,296
[JAO] I just want you
to know that I’m here.

395
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,464
I thought I could fix it.

396
00:19:34,631 --> 00:19:37,426
It doesn’t matter how
long it took you, you got out.

397
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:39,845
- [KARA CRYING SOFTLY]
- [JAO] You saved yourself.

398
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:41,179
So, please, Kara.

399
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:43,515
You have to forgive yourself.
